**********TUTORIAL for Duckduckgo game************
#Before running the program
1.In the kernel/utils/jdbcUtils.java file, please change the PASSWORD into your own password for the database and make
sure your database is connected.
2.Please update the pom.'s dependencies before running the program.
3.Run the "Main" file to run the program.
4.When you enter the login surface, you can unselect the chatBox"cheating mode" to get into the normal game mode.
Also, if you want to register for a new account, just click "register" button and enter your user name and password.
Then, you can see a "user successfully registered" notice with lovely XiaoMai on it!
5.The audio is a little bit low, so please make sure to turn up the video in your device to get better game experience.
6.Click "quit" or  just click the red button on the left top of the surface can quit the program.

#Game rules
1.There are 3 levels for the game. To win the game, you have to kill all the enemies to enter next level.
When each level is finished, you can see "level completed" overlay and just click the continue button to enter
the next level.
2.You can use either "A_W_S_D" or "VK_UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT" to control the motion of the character.
To attack the enemies, you can click your mouse or use "VK_space".
3.There's a cheating mode for the game where you won't die anyway.
4.You can hit the boxes or containers on the floor and there will be potions for you to drink!
5.When you drink the potions, you can add your blood in the game.
6.Enjoy the game!

#features for grading
*basic features
game implementation
a good-looking GUI for users to login and register, which is connected to a database.
*advanced
1.audio for the game
2.animation for the player
3.cheating mode for the player

#implementations
1.GUI
    *I use javafx with css and fxml file to implement a user-friendly login surface for the game. Users can either
 register or login to their accounts. Specifically, by "onAction =" and write the loginViewController, the program
 can respond to the users' request and load the corresponding game mode.
    *The fxml and css files are learned from the demo1 for the "User Management System" given in the tutorial.
    *By learning from the sample given in the tutorials, I write "jdbcUtils" and other functions to check, verify
 and add new accounts which all relate with the database

2.GAME & CHEATINGGAME
    *There are 2 basic modes for the project. I first try to implement the normal game mode. Then change some features
 to get the cheating mode including infinite blood of the players and better-looking game background.
    *For the game class, there are four basic states of the game including MENU/PLAYING/OPTION/QUIT.
 I first set the game panel and game window for the project, in which all the components of the game can be
 updated and drawn.
    *One game is a thread and the "run" function is used for game loop learning from the "multithreading"
 tutorial and game loop tutorial online.
    *In the game class, all the components are initiated including audioOption/audioPlayer/Menu/Playing etc.
    *I split the game into four main states(in the package "state"). Considering the similar structure and methods
 of each states, I write a class and interface (State and Statemethods) for them.{e.g. MENU is a state and has
 statemethods}

3.PLAYING
    *The playing class indicates the playing mode. It includes all the game roles and objects.
    *Game roles: players & enemies
    @players Learning from the website, I first load the player's image and split it into a 2D array. Within the game
 loop, the game constantly update the images and then form the animation for the players. Different actions(jump/run/attack……)
 have different rowIndex. When draw the animation, it actually load all the subimages in a specific row of the array.
    @players player also has its blood and attacking power. The blood for the player can be changed with potion or its motions.

4.UTILZ package
LOADSAVE
    *it is used to save all the images used in the game. Each images has its spring(images.name) and in the "getSpritesAtals" function,
it returns the bufferedImage requested by the String.
CONSTANTS
    *all the basic motions or features are labeled with a constant,which makes it more convenient to call by the program's functions.
constants include all the fixed constants for the game's components such as directions/image.width&height/Gravity/Speed etc.
HelpMethods
    *within this class, all the motions of the character are set. Firstly, the player will get down because of the gravity. Also, he can
not get into the blocks(have to check whether the tiles of the game is solid or not).(decide where he can move)

5.GAME EFFECTS
    *There is rain in the background which may occur.
    *for the background, there are small clouds and big clouds to make the game more beautiful.

6.GAME UI
    *all the game UI have similar implementation structure and that's why buttons inhirit the"PauseButton" class.
 In the PauseButton class, I specify the button's size in the constructor and for each specific button, it should load its own image
 and have its methods.
    *basic methods for the buttons:
    update : update the status
    draw: draw the button on the panel
    mouseOver/mouseClick: check whether the user clicks the button to respond to that

7.OBJECTS
    There are four roles in the game and they all have similar structures to implement. So I write a Entity class
for them to inhirit. All the roles have hitboxs (rectangle). When the rectangle intersects, the enemy can "see the player"
and start to attack.



